            <p>🖤 The Bravery of Hasan (AS) in the Desert of Nineveh and the Trampling of the Body. Prince Qasim (AS) went to the battlefield with such majesty and glory that he displayed an unparalleled example of the bravery of Hasan (AS) and Hussain (AS), overturning the ranks of the enemies. He was a young boy, but he attacked the enemies as fearlessly as the Lion of God's uncle, Hazrat Hamza (AS), had done in Badr and Uhud. When the enemy could not face him directly, a wretched man, on the orders of Umar ibn Sa'ad, sneakily attacked from behind, and a dagger and spear pierced the delicate side of Prince Qasim (AS). The strike of the spear reminded the prince of the wounded side of his grieving grandmother, Lady Fatima Zahra (SA)! The prince agonizingly fell from the saddle onto the land of Karbala and called out to his Master: "O dear Uncle! Come to Qasim's aid..."</p>
            
