      <p>Since 1948, when Palestine was occupied, this issue has existed with great sensitivity from the very beginning. When the Palestinians themselves achieved victory against the Zionists in the Battle of Karameh, they proposed a certain day in October to be declared 'Palestine Day,' but it did not receive significant acceptance. The founder of the Islamic Revolution of Iran, Imam Khomeini (RA), from the very beginning of his struggles, declared Palestine's liberation and its occupation illegitimate. After the success of the Islamic Revolution in Iran, relations with Israel were severed, and its embassy was handed over to the Palestinians. When Israel attacked southern Lebanon, Imam Khomeini (RA), through a message on the 13th of Ramadan, declared the last Friday of Ramadan as Quds Day:</p>
