    image: 'https://res.cloudinary.com/dlafcjt6z/image/upload/v1783929558/columns_fpkl28.png',
    content: `
      <p><strong>The Impact of the Islamic Revolution of Iran</strong></p>
      <p><strong>By: Shabbir Ahmed Shigri</strong></p>
      <p>The revolution that came under the patronage of Imam Khomeini (RA) will always be remembered in history. This Islamic Revolution that occurred in Iran is immortal and unique in every aspect, and it would perhaps not be an exaggeration to say that it is an unparalleled revolution in the history of Islam and Iran. The unique characteristics of Iran's Islamic Revolution distinguish it from other revolutions in the world. In the twentieth century, the Russian Revolution occurred, and before that, in the eighteenth century, the French Revolution occurred. However, they lost their effect very quickly. The effects of the French and Russian revolutions are not even seen within their own countries; rather, these revolutions can only be read about in books.</p>
      <p>In the French Revolution, leaders like Lafayette and Danton presented themselves as leaders, but none of them completely led the French Revolution during the movement and in the years following its success. Similarly, in the Russian Revolution in the twentieth century, although Lenin's face emerged as a leader, he had no role in overthrowing the Romanov government.</p>
      <p>The Russian Revolution was not ideological, nor was its leader. These people emerged after the revolution. Similarly, in the French Revolution, ideology played no role; it was a revolution against the Church. But when we look at the Islamic Revolution of Iran, we see great leaders like Imam Khomeini (RA) leading it. His divine personality is what distinguishes Iran's Islamic Revolution from other revolutions, because a personality like Imam Khomeini (RA) is not seen in any other revolution.</p>
      <p>Iran's Islamic Revolution is the name of a movement led by an unparalleled philosopher. Such issues that handled the reins of this revolution from the beginning and, after its success, protected it from all kinds of harm and entrusted it to future generations. Imam Khomeini (RA) was trained in the school of the Ahl al-Bayt and the Quran. He advanced the Islamic Revolution under the shadow of the teachings of Islam and the Ahl al-Bayt. Ten years after the success of the revolution, he protected it from various storms and conspiracies and made it universal. When we talk about the Russian Revolution, when it occurred, not only its own government but no government in the world opposed it, because the Russian government's enmities, wars with the Ottomans and Japanese, led everyone to support the revolutionaries. In Austria, Russia, and other countries, due to prolonged wars, everyone supported the revolutions. However, Iran's Islamic Revolution occurred under conditions where all major powers of the East and West were fully supporting the Shah's government and were making every effort to prevent the revolution from succeeding. Thus, all major powers of the world united and waged a war against Iran that lasted for a year and a half, in which Iran's brave people achieved victory.</p>
      <p>The most important slogan of Iran's Islamic Revolution was based on opposition to imperialism. It made its identity through this slogan: "Neither East nor West. We are not in any bloc. Rather, we will establish an Islamic Republic system based on Islamic teachings." That is why, at that time and even today, observers of the world say that Iran's Islamic Revolution succeeded in a world where it was being attacked from all sides. Despite this, the Islamic Revolution broke the back of internal tyranny and foreign imperialism at a time when no power in the world was with the Iranian people. The Islamic Revolution has countless characteristics, one of which was its unwavering and clear stance. The Islamic Revolution of Iran and Imam Khomeini (RA) were at such a height that, even after such a long time, people from Asia to Europe and from Africa to Latin America are seeing Imam Khomeini's (RA) statement in practice and are themselves saying that the world's biggest Satan is America. The Islamic Revolution has, in the past years, proven this truth.</p>
    `
